; Interprets: RFC 4072
;; What RFC 4072's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. A block on the DER or DEA binds the document's print of
;; them under the Diameter EAP application (5), which no other document's
;; print shares, RFC 5778's and TS 29.273's among them; a block with no
;; scope holds wherever a document reading the AVP reads it
;; (docs/constraints.md, Precedence). What the server decides, the EAP
;; packet inside the EAP-Payload and an earlier message are not read, so a
;; rule resting on them is `text-only`.


;; Whether an error is fatal is the server's, by the EAP Type it did not
;; understand; a failure Result-Code has other causes.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dea-fatal-error-eap-failure
; AVP: EAP-Payload
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Section: 2.4
"A Diameter server determining that a fatal error has occurred MUST send a Diameter-EAP-Answer with a failure Result-Code and an EAP-Payload AVP encapsulating an EAP Failure packet."
    text-only


;; The non-fatal error's answer is the one with DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH
;; and no EAP-Payload, as the paragraph after it reads it; every other
;; round's answer carries its EAP Request.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dea-non-fatal-error-reissued-payload
; AVP: EAP-Reissued-Payload
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Section: 2.4
"A Diameter server determining that a non-fatal error has occurred MUST send a Diameter-EAP-Answer with DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH Result-Code, but no EAP-Payload AVP."
"To simplify RADIUS translation, this message MUST also include an EAP-Reissued-Payload AVP encapsulating the previous EAP Request sent by the server."
    present-if Result-Code = DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH and not EAP-Payload


;; The EAP packet's Code, the EAP-Payload's first octet, which no condition
;; reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dea-eap-result-not-multi-round
; AVP: Result-Code
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Section: 2.8.2
"A Diameter-EAP-Answer message containing an EAP-Payload of type EAP-Success or EAP-Failure MUST NOT have the Result-Code AVP set to DIAMETER_MULTI_ROUND_AUTH."
    text-only


;; The answer's: the request always holds an EAP-Payload, and table 5.1
;; gives its Reply-Message "0", read below.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: dea-reply-message-without-eap-payload
; AVP: Reply-Message
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Answer
; Section: 2.8.3
"The Reply-Message AVP [NASREQ] MUST NOT be included in any Diameter message containing an EAP-Payload AVP."
    excludes EAP-Payload


;; As section 2.8.2's: the EAP packet's Code.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-eap-payload-no-eap-request
; AVP: EAP-Payload
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 2.8.4
"A Diameter client MUST NOT send a Diameter-EAP-Request encapsulating an EAP Request packet, and a Diameter server receiving such a packet MUST respond with a failure Result-Code."
    text-only


;; The State AVPs of the answer before, an earlier message.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-state-from-the-dea
; AVP: State
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 3.1
"A subsequent DER message MUST include any State AVPs [NASREQ] that were present in the DEA."
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-eap-key-name-empty
; AVP: EAP-Key-Name
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 4.1.4
"As a result, a Key-Name AVP sent in a Diameter-EAP-Request MUST NOT contain any data."
    length 0 octets


;; Table 5.1's DER column: what its "0" says the Diameter-EAP-Request
;; never carries, an AVP its body admits only through * [ AVP ]. The table
;; spells RFC 4005's Framed-AppleTalk-Link, -Network and -Zone
;; Framed-Appletalk-.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-accounting-eap-auth-method-table-absent
; AVP: Accounting-EAP-Auth-Method
; Command: Diameter-EAP-Request
; Section: 5.1
"0 The AVP MUST NOT be present in the message"
"Accounting-EAP-Auth-Method | 0 | 0+ |"
    absent


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: der-acct-interim-interval-table-absent
; AVP: Acct-Interim-Interval
